{
  "description": "The corpus documents against the published census (GORILA 1,427 + RILA-S1 107 = 1,534). Every document falls in exactly one class, taken in this order: outside the Linear A area (by site), RILA-S1 accepted, RILA-S1 doubtful, RILA-S1 listed but not counted, published after 2023, outside both editions, GORILA labelled (source_provenance), GORILA unlabelled, unresolved. RILA-S1 sets are keyed by RILA-S1's own sigla (Del Freo & Zurbach 2024, pp. xxvii–xxxv, xlv–xlvii) and list the corpus keys holding each; an empty list means the corpus does not hold it. The document sets hold document ids (sides folded). gorila_unlabelled records GORILA V's general concordance for documents held under no GORILA label; an id that has since gained a label is counted as labelled. merged maps a second record of an object to the record it was folded into. gorila_v records how GORILA V's general concordance (pp. 83–113) falls into the classes: the GORILA documents RILA-S1 edits again among its accepted 107 or its doubtful list, and the records that hold two GORILA sigla.",
